# Captain preferences

Copy this file to `~/.local/share/firstmate/data/captain.md` and fill it in.
It is per host and is never committed.

## Communication language

- The captain communicates in Vietnamese; Firstmate and crew reply in Vietnamese.

## Working style

- The captain is a senior AI integration engineer working mainly with Python,
  C++, DeepStream, CUDA and GStreamer, and occasionally on small full-stack
  tools (backend, frontend and MongoDB).
- <This host's hardware: NVIDIA GPU or not; which GPU or Jetson device must be
  used to verify GPU-dependent work.>
- Each server's Firstmate manages only its own crews; no cross-server crew
  management.
- The daily-use dotfiles checkout is `~/dotfiles`, separate from Firstmate's
  own clone. After a dotfiles merge changes live config or mods, offer to
  fast-forward that checkout with `ff-only`, preserving uncommitted edits.
  Proceed only on the captain's word for that specific update.

## Delivery preferences

- PR descriptions contain no external tool links or attribution: no
  "Generated with Claude Code" line, "Updates from git push no-mistakes" footer,
  or local `~/.no-mistakes/...` paths. Do not leave a no-mistakes attestation
  comment. Workers strip these after the final pipeline push.

## Credentials rule

<How agents must treat secrets: never print or commit them, where they may be
read from, and what to do when one is needed.>
